Suggests: network-manager-openvpn3-gnome
Description: network management framework (OpenVPN 3 plugin core)
 NetworkManager is a system network service that manages your network
 devices and connections. This package lets NetworkManager start and
 stop VPN connections through the OpenVPN 3 Linux client (openvpn3),
 so openvpn3 profiles show up in the desktop's standard VPN menu and in
 nmcli.
 .
 This package contains the desktop-independent core: the NetworkManager
 service, the libnm plugin used by nmcli and the desktop editors to import
 and export OpenVPN profiles, and the helper secret agents run to learn
 which passwords and one-time codes to ask for.

Package: network-manager-openvpn3-gnome
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         network-manager-openvpn3 (= ${binary:Version}),
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0
Description: network management framework (OpenVPN 3 plugin GNOME GUI)
 NetworkManager is a system network service that manages your network
 devices and connections. This package lets NetworkManager start and
 stop VPN connections through the OpenVPN 3 Linux client (openvpn3).
 .
 This package contains the connection editors: GTK 4 for GNOME Settings
 and GTK 3 for nm-connection-editor (also used on Xfce, MATE, Cinnamon and
 other desktops running nm-applet), and the password dialog nm-applet shows.
